    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** leads the squad with an elite 78.75 score. Despite a dynamic platoon disadvantage against the lefty Nick Lodolo, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a massive 17% SP skill boost and a prime #2 spot in the order, making him our primary engine for SB and run production. **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Isaac Paredes** serve as our secondary pillars, both scoring well above 65. **Vinnie Pasquantino** draws a highly favorable matchup against the righty Troy Melton, while **Isaac Paredes** utilizes a 9% platoon advantage and the batting order stability of the #3 hole to provide a high floor for RBI potential.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved our bench, specifically regarding the exclusion of **Cole Young**. While **Cole Young** provides a high-upside profile for stolen bases, his 47.73 score was ultimately suppressed by a bottom-third of the order projection and a matchup against a lefty in Matthew Boyd. We opted to prioritize the high-volume plate appearances of **Henry Bolte** at the #1 spot and **Mickey Moniak**, who\u2014despite his own platoon issues against a lefty\u2014benefits from a massive 14% park factor boost. Our depth remains challenged by the high caliber of opposing arms like Chris Sale, who effectively neutralized the potential value of **Brice Turang** and forced his benching to preserve our game caps.\n\nRisks for the day are dominated by the \"Lineup Pending\" status across the board, as our projected scores are contingent on the stability of those assigned batting positions. Should **Gabriel Moreno** drop out of the #3 spot or **Henry Bolte** lose his lead-off duties, we will be forced to re-evaluate our utility efficiency. Furthermore, while **Jose Caballero** maintains a strong platoon advantage against the lefty Mason Fluharty, his projection is hampered by a significant -8% penalty for his assumed #9 spot in the order, requiring a high degree of defensive efficiency to justify the start over options like **Griffin Conine** or **Austin Riley**.",
